1
00:02:03,732 --> 00:02:08,542
No animals were harmed during
the filming of this series.

2
00:02:09,109 --> 00:02:12,759
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

3
00:02:14,454 --> 00:02:15,774
Alps!

4
00:02:15,786 --> 00:02:17,096
Brothers!

5
00:02:17,580 --> 00:02:19,240
-Brothers!
-Brothers!

6
00:02:19,357 --> 00:02:20,497
Brothers!

7
00:02:22,891 --> 00:02:24,211
We are here brothers!

8
00:02:24,670 --> 00:02:26,739
-Hang on!
-Hang on, brothers!

9
00:02:26,739 --> 00:02:28,359
We are here!

10
00:02:35,678 --> 00:02:38,288
-My Alps!
-Brothers, make a sound!

11
00:02:39,314 --> 00:02:41,304
-Come on!
-Come on!

12
00:02:46,012 --> 00:02:47,672
My Bey!

13
00:02:53,542 --> 00:02:55,472
My Bey, this won't open!

14
00:02:56,205 --> 00:02:58,525
Brothers!
Hang on!

15
00:02:58,824 --> 00:03:00,284
My Bey!

16
00:03:02,255 --> 00:03:03,635
My Bey!

17
00:03:09,087 --> 00:03:10,597
It is stuck, my Bey!

18
00:03:11,035 --> 00:03:12,692
Alps!

19
00:03:12,692 --> 00:03:13,952
-I won't let go!
-My Bey!

20
00:03:13,952 --> 00:03:15,812
I won't leave my Alps!

21
00:03:18,906 --> 00:03:20,906
-Alps!
-My Bey!

22
00:03:20,944 --> 00:03:22,264
Alps!

23
00:03:23,463 --> 00:03:26,793
There must be another way out!

24
00:03:27,073 --> 00:03:29,183
-We will find it, my Bey.
-Come on!

25
00:03:29,549 --> 00:03:32,022
-We will find it.
-Come on!

26
00:03:46,257 --> 00:03:47,587
Come on, Alps!

27
00:03:49,346 --> 00:03:51,786
-Here!
-Osman!

28
00:04:14,269 --> 00:04:16,168
Your Alps are dead!

29
00:04:16,197 --> 00:04:17,887
You will die too!

30
00:04:19,903 --> 00:04:22,920
-Come on! Come on!
-Come on! Let's find a way out!

31
00:04:22,920 --> 00:04:25,179
-Come on! Come on!
-Come on! Come on!

32
00:04:25,179 --> 00:04:27,519
-Come on!
-Come on!

33
00:04:27,767 --> 00:04:30,357
-Come on!
-Come on!

34
00:04:37,848 --> 00:04:39,528
Alps!

35
00:04:40,606 --> 00:04:41,996
Brothers!

36
00:04:41,996 --> 00:04:43,616
Attack!

37
00:04:44,712 --> 00:04:46,382
Allahu Akbar!

38
00:05:02,735 --> 00:05:04,905
Brothers! Are you all right!

39
00:05:06,517 --> 00:05:07,737
Brothers!

40
00:05:10,768 --> 00:05:12,648
Gencebay! Take this, brother!

41
00:05:13,432 --> 00:05:16,212
Come on!
Come on, Saltuk!

42
00:05:20,103 --> 00:05:21,693
Let me help.

43
00:05:23,688 --> 00:05:26,148
I'm here!
I am not dead!

44
00:05:36,246 --> 00:05:37,416
Come on!

45
00:05:39,158 --> 00:05:40,708
-Come on!
-Come on!

46
00:05:41,978 --> 00:05:43,178
Come on! Let's go!

47
00:05:57,136 --> 00:05:58,576
My Bey!

48
00:05:59,116 --> 00:06:00,786
Brothers!

49
00:06:02,445 --> 00:06:04,735
Come on, brothers!
Come on!

50
00:06:14,872 --> 00:06:16,372
Brothers!

51
00:06:23,933 --> 00:06:25,585
-Boran!
-My Bey!

52
00:06:25,585 --> 00:06:27,235
Come here!

53
00:06:44,731 --> 00:06:45,891
My Bey.

54
00:06:46,282 --> 00:06:48,012
Some Alps couldn't make it.

55
00:06:48,084 --> 00:06:49,464
There are many casualties.

56
00:06:54,870 --> 00:06:56,260
Come on.

57
00:07:01,329 --> 00:07:02,909
My brothers!

58
00:07:05,978 --> 00:07:07,838
You bastard!

59
00:07:13,851 --> 00:07:15,701
-Let me go! I won't come!
-Walk! Walk!

60
00:07:17,148 --> 00:07:18,918
Don't make this harder!

61
00:07:20,128 --> 00:07:23,408
You are forcing her! Let her go!

62
00:07:23,725 --> 00:07:25,765
I made so many preparations.

63
00:07:28,073 --> 00:07:30,383
I will marry Mari.

64
00:07:33,104 --> 00:07:35,844
Don't you see!
Mari doesn't want you!

65
00:07:36,775 --> 00:07:39,139
This should be between you and me.

66
00:07:39,139 --> 00:07:41,749
Let her go, Kosses!

67
00:07:43,577 --> 00:07:45,627
Don't hurt him!

68
00:07:47,135 --> 00:07:48,575
Nikola!

69
00:07:49,197 --> 00:07:50,697
All right, Nikola!

70
00:07:50,749 --> 00:07:52,959
Please don't hurt him!

71
00:07:52,994 --> 00:07:55,994
I wanted to run away. He just helped!

72
00:07:56,008 --> 00:07:58,798
Please, brother! Please!

73
00:07:58,873 --> 00:08:01,063
Nikola, please!

74
00:08:04,313 --> 00:08:06,303
So he just helped?

75
00:08:08,391 --> 00:08:10,481
I can't even recognize you anymore, Mari.

76
00:08:11,223 --> 00:08:13,493
What did this man do to you!

77
00:08:15,680 --> 00:08:18,830
How can you ask for help from our
enemy, Mari? How?

78
00:08:20,596 --> 00:08:23,266
How could you, Kosses?

79
00:08:24,816 --> 00:08:28,716
What kind of a brother are you to do this
to your sister?

80
00:08:32,010 --> 00:08:35,210
But don't worry. Your time will come too.

81
00:08:37,546 --> 00:08:41,527
I will ask you to account for every tear
you made her shed.

82
00:08:41,527 --> 00:08:46,237
If I am Turgut Bey, I will be your executioner
and put you through hell!

83
00:08:46,237 --> 00:08:48,787
Hell!

84
00:08:49,593 --> 00:08:52,203
No, brother!
Don't! Please!

85
00:08:57,097 --> 00:08:58,337
You...

86
00:08:58,672 --> 00:08:59,972
...will be dead...

87
00:09:00,511 --> 00:09:02,331
...today!

88
00:09:05,899 --> 00:09:07,299
Your death will be...

89
00:09:07,997 --> 00:09:09,957
...by our hands!

90
00:09:16,267 --> 00:09:19,567
Dreams, dreams, Turgut Bey!

91
00:09:21,813 --> 00:09:24,953
You've ruined the best day of my life.

92
00:09:27,502 --> 00:09:29,542
I will kill you...

93
00:09:29,812 --> 00:09:32,052
...in such a way that...

94
00:09:32,206 --> 00:09:34,806
...it will be an example for all
my enemies.

95
00:09:34,876 --> 00:09:36,796
-An example.
-Kill me.

96
00:09:39,214 --> 00:09:41,044
Kill me!

97
00:09:41,645 --> 00:09:44,095
Or I will make you regret it, Nikola!

98
00:09:44,312 --> 00:09:45,522
Nikola!

99
00:09:46,107 --> 00:09:49,044
All right! Let him go. If you let him go
without any harm...

100
00:09:49,044 --> 00:09:52,354
...I promise I will marry you.

101
00:09:54,294 --> 00:09:55,924
Don't do this, Mari!

102
00:09:56,298 --> 00:09:58,248
-Don't do this.
-Shut up.

103
00:09:59,411 --> 00:10:01,281
Don't say such things.

104
00:10:01,293 --> 00:10:04,903
If I am alive, I won't let you go to this
tyrant.

105
00:10:07,106 --> 00:10:08,866
Dear Mari.

106
00:10:09,772 --> 00:10:12,232
You will marry me anyway.

107
00:10:16,169 --> 00:10:17,821
Why would I let him go?

108
00:10:17,821 --> 00:10:19,521
You bastard!

109
00:10:20,847 --> 00:10:22,317
Enough.

110
00:10:22,692 --> 00:10:24,122
Let's have some fun.

111
00:10:25,172 --> 00:10:26,612
Get him up.

112
00:10:26,811 --> 00:10:30,121
Stop! Nikola don't!
Nikola, please, don't!

113
00:10:30,356 --> 00:10:33,396
- Brother, please help!
-Enough!

114
00:10:33,638 --> 00:10:35,608
Enough!
Enough.

115
00:10:39,797 --> 00:10:41,317
Let Mari go.

116
00:10:43,849 --> 00:10:45,459
Tie him up!

117
00:10:48,459 --> 00:10:49,869
Tie.

118
00:10:50,041 --> 00:10:51,431
Tie me up, Nikola!

119
00:10:51,554 --> 00:10:53,664
Do your best.

120
00:10:54,555 --> 00:10:56,015
But know that...

121
00:10:58,246 --> 00:11:00,456
...even if you marry Mari...

122
00:11:01,249 --> 00:11:05,039
...she will never want you.

123
00:11:08,232 --> 00:11:10,632
Take his clothes off too.

124
00:11:56,775 --> 00:11:58,925
Look at this!

125
00:12:02,914 --> 00:12:04,994
You don't grow in here but...

126
00:12:05,869 --> 00:12:07,819
...I am sure there is a reason.

127
00:12:24,373 --> 00:12:26,203
In the name of Allah.

128
00:12:28,372 --> 00:12:30,252
Nikola! Don't!

129
00:12:33,835 --> 00:12:36,805
Brother! Nikola don't!

130
00:12:43,036 --> 00:12:44,646
Nikola.

131
00:12:47,861 --> 00:12:49,691
I must get help.

132
00:12:50,148 --> 00:12:51,678
I must go to the tribe at once.

133
00:12:53,032 --> 00:12:55,422
Brother, please do something!

134
00:13:39,788 --> 00:13:41,208
Boran!

135
00:13:51,076 --> 00:13:53,556
Take him! Take him!

136
00:13:56,240 --> 00:13:57,720
Retreat!

137
00:13:57,797 --> 00:13:59,217
Retreat!

138
00:14:02,744 --> 00:14:04,734
-Boran!
-Brother!

139
00:14:07,032 --> 00:14:08,802
Boran!

140
00:14:11,493 --> 00:14:12,723
My Bey!

141
00:14:13,909 --> 00:14:15,169
My Bey, stop!

142
00:14:15,929 --> 00:14:17,259
My Bey!

143
00:14:17,270 --> 00:14:18,440
My Bey!

144
00:14:24,979 --> 00:14:26,359
My Bey, stop!

145
00:14:35,421 --> 00:14:37,121
My Bey.

146
00:14:37,158 --> 00:14:39,998
They are alive!
They are injured!

147
00:14:41,208 --> 00:14:42,798
They are injured!

148
00:14:47,705 --> 00:14:49,255
Brother!

149
00:14:50,993 --> 00:14:52,493
Brother!

150
00:15:05,222 --> 00:15:07,372
-Brother.
-Brother.

151
00:15:07,773 --> 00:15:10,013
I won't let them take you.

152
00:15:21,419 --> 00:15:22,919
Look at these.

153
00:15:27,024 --> 00:15:29,804
Tell me, Bala.
How do you feel?

154
00:15:32,627 --> 00:15:34,567
Do you think it is a girl or a boy?

155
00:15:36,658 --> 00:15:38,188
I don't know.

156
00:15:38,838 --> 00:15:40,258
As long as it is healthy.

157
00:15:43,542 --> 00:15:45,862
Mother, what do you think?

158
00:15:46,247 --> 00:15:48,987
My mother has made many correct
guesses.

159
00:15:50,584 --> 00:15:54,114
I don't know. I feel like it's a boy.

160
00:15:58,064 --> 00:16:00,414
As long as it is healthy.

161
00:16:01,014 --> 00:16:02,804
I hope.

162
00:16:04,489 --> 00:16:06,179
Come in!

163
00:16:09,140 --> 00:16:10,730
Kumral Abdal.

164
00:16:13,512 --> 00:16:16,808
Turgut Bey and the Lord's sister
got caught by the Lord...

165
00:16:16,808 --> 00:16:18,818
...as they were running away.

166
00:16:21,629 --> 00:16:23,949
The situation is terrible, Selcen Hatun.

167
00:16:25,998 --> 00:16:27,450
They will kill him.

168
00:16:27,450 --> 00:16:28,930
What are you saying?

169
00:16:29,083 --> 00:16:31,053
-Inform Gündüz immediately!
-Mother.

170
00:16:31,180 --> 00:16:33,122
Gündüz is at Söğüt.

171
00:16:33,122 --> 00:16:34,798
What will we do?

172
00:16:34,798 --> 00:16:36,788
A Bey's Hatun is here, mother!

173
00:16:37,161 --> 00:16:40,361
I won't let those heathens take Turgut
or Mari.

174
00:16:41,285 --> 00:16:44,545
Aygül, get the Alps ready. We must hurry.

175
00:16:45,332 --> 00:16:47,602
Don't worry, mother.

176
00:16:49,604 --> 00:16:52,544
What about Turgut Bey's Alps?

177
00:16:52,786 --> 00:16:54,546
There were none.

178
00:16:55,076 --> 00:16:58,016
You find them, Kumral Abdal.

179
00:16:58,162 --> 00:17:00,062
You know where they are.

180
00:17:01,721 --> 00:17:04,381
-Mother.
-Protect yourselves, my girl.

181
00:17:12,159 --> 00:17:13,769
Nikola, stop.

182
00:17:13,836 --> 00:17:15,915
Nikola, stop!

183
00:17:17,843 --> 00:17:20,563
He will pay, Mari!
He will!

184
00:17:23,692 --> 00:17:25,281
He will!

185
00:17:30,129 --> 00:17:31,609
Give it to me!

186
00:17:32,829 --> 00:17:34,799
He won't die peacefully.

187
00:17:36,966 --> 00:17:39,426
You won't die peacefully, Turgut.

188
00:17:41,286 --> 00:17:42,876
No, Nikola!

189
00:17:43,274 --> 00:17:46,504
Do you think these feet can walk?

190
00:17:49,435 --> 00:17:52,455
Nikola! I am begging you!
Please, stop!

191
00:17:56,900 --> 00:17:58,310
Give it to me!

192
00:18:01,034 --> 00:18:03,384
Let them do what they want, Mari.

193
00:18:04,174 --> 00:18:06,684
Please, don't beg these bastards.

194
00:18:10,351 --> 00:18:13,561
You made a big mistake, Turgut.
A huge mistake!

195
00:18:36,815 --> 00:18:40,155
Come on, cut my hand.

196
00:18:40,315 --> 00:18:42,135
Then speak.

197
00:18:44,347 --> 00:18:45,597
Or...

198
00:18:46,945 --> 00:18:49,665
...aren't you man enough, Nikola?

199
00:18:50,989 --> 00:18:55,269
I will cut your tongue, Turgut!

200
00:18:58,149 --> 00:19:02,039
Then you won't speak and cross the line.

201
00:19:08,537 --> 00:19:09,947
It's okay.

202
00:19:10,070 --> 00:19:11,080
Look at me.

203
00:19:12,054 --> 00:19:15,993
Let speaking to what's mine...

204
00:19:15,993 --> 00:19:19,262
...if you even look at what's mine...

205
00:19:19,272 --> 00:19:21,402
...I will carve out your eyes!

206
00:19:23,788 --> 00:19:25,518
Do you understand?
I will carve them!

207
00:19:27,489 --> 00:19:29,199
Look, Mari.

208
00:19:29,790 --> 00:19:33,340
This is what you get when you make
the wrong decision.

209
00:19:37,217 --> 00:19:41,087
Let me go! I hate you!

210
00:19:42,276 --> 00:19:44,066
My dear wife Mari.

211
00:19:44,300 --> 00:19:47,591
You always ask me why I don't
do what you desire.

212
00:19:47,591 --> 00:19:49,971
Why I don't ask for your opinion.

213
00:19:50,621 --> 00:19:53,371
Now I am asking. Should I...

214
00:19:53,519 --> 00:19:57,059
...cut Turgut's tongue or carve out his
eyes?

215
00:19:59,217 --> 00:20:01,127
I am not your wife!

216
00:20:01,484 --> 00:20:03,505
I hate you!
I hate you!

217
00:20:03,505 --> 00:20:05,725
-I hate you!
-Enough!

218
00:20:28,473 --> 00:20:30,023
Nikola, stop!

219
00:21:36,900 --> 00:21:38,570
Brothers.

220
00:21:46,607 --> 00:21:48,547
May Allah be pleased with you, brother.

221
00:22:07,427 --> 00:22:09,907
There is no one else inside, my Bey.

222
00:22:09,934 --> 00:22:11,314
What is your order?

223
00:22:17,833 --> 00:22:19,333
My Bey.

224
00:22:21,694 --> 00:22:23,784
My brother's compass is here.

225
00:22:25,643 --> 00:22:27,513
But he is taken by heathens.

226
00:22:37,988 --> 00:22:40,038
We will take Boran from them...

227
00:22:41,845 --> 00:22:44,295
...as we took their property.

228
00:22:46,660 --> 00:22:48,820
All of their time will come.

229
00:22:49,330 --> 00:22:50,940
All of them.

230
00:22:51,491 --> 00:22:55,281
We'll make them pay for
both the captives and our martyrs.

231
00:22:58,082 --> 00:23:00,812
Bay Sungur and the other Alps will not
let anyone...

232
00:23:01,164 --> 00:23:05,694
...take a step in the mines except us.

233
00:23:07,824 --> 00:23:09,504
We will go and...

234
00:23:09,931 --> 00:23:12,141
...bury our martyrs.

235
00:23:19,898 --> 00:23:21,578
Come on, Alps.

236
00:23:44,898 --> 00:23:47,008
Turgut Bey's Alps were looking for him.

237
00:23:47,336 --> 00:23:48,706
Aygül, come on.

238
00:23:48,706 --> 00:23:50,336
Be careful.
Come on!

239
00:23:52,045 --> 00:23:53,835
Let's go!

240
00:24:05,479 --> 00:24:09,799
I will make you suffer every pain a person
can suffer.

241
00:24:14,492 --> 00:24:15,273
Every pain!

242
00:24:15,273 --> 00:24:16,463
No, Nikola!

243
00:24:17,020 --> 00:24:18,530
Every pain!

244
00:24:18,576 --> 00:24:19,916
Nikola, stop!

245
00:24:24,033 --> 00:24:25,443
Mari?

246
00:24:25,735 --> 00:24:26,945
What is it?

247
00:24:27,515 --> 00:24:30,535
Do you feel sorry for this shepherd?

248
00:24:41,268 --> 00:24:43,168
I will break every bone you have.

249
00:24:44,535 --> 00:24:46,365
Brother, do something!
He will die!

250
00:24:50,315 --> 00:24:51,975
This is enough.

251
00:24:53,833 --> 00:24:55,343
Enough!

252
00:24:57,498 --> 00:24:59,898
Let me go! Damn it!

253
00:24:59,905 --> 00:25:01,855
Shut up, Mari!
Enough!

254
00:25:03,813 --> 00:25:05,793
Mari...

255
00:25:08,628 --> 00:25:10,148
This is the end.

256
00:25:10,766 --> 00:25:13,356
The end of Turgut Bey.

257
00:25:13,739 --> 00:25:15,869
-No!
-Yes.

258
00:25:16,705 --> 00:25:18,645
-No, Nikola!
-Yes!

259
00:25:19,073 --> 00:25:20,263
No, Nikola!

260
00:25:20,343 --> 00:25:22,323
I am looking for the world.

261
00:25:23,792 --> 00:25:26,342
Do you know where it is?

262
00:25:48,024 --> 00:25:50,244
You smell like the world.

263
00:25:52,167 --> 00:25:55,977
We were losing a lunatic. You came.
Now we are complete.

264
00:25:56,642 --> 00:25:58,732
What do you want, lunatic?

265
00:26:00,974 --> 00:26:03,014
The lovers don't die.

266
00:26:11,827 --> 00:26:14,017
The lovers don't die!

267
00:26:16,657 --> 00:26:18,637
I am here, Turgut Bey!

268
00:26:19,691 --> 00:26:21,021
Mari!

269
00:26:39,778 --> 00:26:41,108
Mari!

270
00:26:42,878 --> 00:26:43,845
Come on!

271
00:26:43,845 --> 00:26:45,155
Mari!

272
00:27:06,750 --> 00:27:08,070
Mari!

273
00:27:09,982 --> 00:27:11,512
Turgut, come on!

274
00:27:11,522 --> 00:27:13,932
No, no! Let go!
Come on!

275
00:27:27,706 --> 00:27:29,276
Attack!

276
00:27:29,713 --> 00:27:30,952
Here!

277
00:27:30,952 --> 00:27:32,862
Mari, watch out!

278
00:28:00,018 --> 00:28:01,558
Nikola!

279
00:28:04,328 --> 00:28:05,918
Turgut!

280
00:28:11,697 --> 00:28:13,467
Turgut!

281
00:28:16,937 --> 00:28:19,627
Get out of my way!
You useless piece of--

282
00:28:20,634 --> 00:28:22,084
Get out!

283
00:30:27,420 --> 00:30:30,880
You are oppressed under the
reign of chaos.

284
00:30:31,868 --> 00:30:34,128
You need order.

285
00:30:35,022 --> 00:30:38,532
A strong head is needed
for that order.

286
00:30:39,435 --> 00:30:41,075
I'm that head.

287
00:30:41,430 --> 00:30:44,160
The Vizier of the Great Seljuks,
Alemşah!

288
00:30:49,324 --> 00:30:53,294
These borders are now
under my rule.

289
00:30:54,125 --> 00:30:55,535
Onur.

290
00:30:57,183 --> 00:31:00,543
Is Lord Nikola informed of my arrival?

291
00:31:00,878 --> 00:31:02,778
I sent a messenger, my vizier.

292
00:31:02,944 --> 00:31:04,674
Lord Nikola awaits you.

293
00:31:05,673 --> 00:31:07,646
I'll go to him first.

294
00:31:07,646 --> 00:31:09,656
Then to Kayı Tribe.

295
00:31:11,412 --> 00:31:14,982
I'll see the rebel named
Osman in his home.

296
00:31:15,229 --> 00:31:19,419
Let's see who is this
famous Osman.

297
00:31:23,650 --> 00:31:26,610
Osman or the lords, make no
difference.

298
00:31:27,116 --> 00:31:30,526
They all will change their politics.

299
00:31:31,528 --> 00:31:34,898
Now, the only truth on these lands...

300
00:31:35,632 --> 00:31:37,432
is my word.

301
00:31:37,712 --> 00:31:40,592
They all will learn this.

302
00:31:53,654 --> 00:31:55,784
Slowly. Slowly.

303
00:31:59,651 --> 00:32:01,901
Turgut Bey!
Mari!

304
00:32:04,046 --> 00:32:05,416
Are you alright?

305
00:32:08,838 --> 00:32:10,228
Malhun Hatun.

306
00:32:10,411 --> 00:32:11,671
Aygül.

307
00:32:11,907 --> 00:32:14,027
They came in time.

308
00:32:14,570 --> 00:32:15,940
Thank you.

309
00:32:22,306 --> 00:32:23,566
Son.

310
00:32:25,269 --> 00:32:27,149
Your wounds are severe.

311
00:32:27,203 --> 00:32:29,453
You need to go to the infirmary.

312
00:32:30,414 --> 00:32:32,164
I will but...

313
00:32:33,755 --> 00:32:35,095
Osman Bey...

314
00:32:35,602 --> 00:32:37,452
any news from him?

315
00:32:37,463 --> 00:32:38,823
Where is he?

316
00:33:00,950 --> 00:33:02,790
My Allah protect him.

317
00:33:37,888 --> 00:33:39,368
Cerkutay!

318
00:33:40,359 --> 00:33:42,448
Cerkutay!

319
00:33:46,577 --> 00:33:48,177
My Allah protect us!

320
00:34:01,475 --> 00:34:02,795
My bey.

321
00:34:17,608 --> 00:34:19,568
Cerkutay. Cerkutay, thank Allah!

322
00:34:20,010 --> 00:34:22,250
You are here!
Thank Allah!

323
00:34:25,445 --> 00:34:26,935
Osman?

324
00:34:26,943 --> 00:34:28,223
Are you alright?

325
00:34:40,592 --> 00:34:42,293
Turgut Bey.

326
00:34:45,395 --> 00:34:47,085
Are you alright?

327
00:34:47,712 --> 00:34:50,262
You ask about me, Osman Bey.

328
00:34:51,248 --> 00:34:53,069
I'm alright, thank Allah.

329
00:34:53,446 --> 00:34:55,045
But you?

330
00:34:59,109 --> 00:35:00,429
How?

331
00:35:06,923 --> 00:35:09,423
The mine belongs to the Kayı now.

332
00:35:13,895 --> 00:35:16,005
But we have martyrs.

333
00:35:20,668 --> 00:35:22,648
My brother Boran...

334
00:35:23,892 --> 00:35:26,312
is captured by Rogatus.

335
00:35:30,195 --> 00:35:31,585
My bey.

336
00:35:32,782 --> 00:35:35,752
The land becomes home when
it gets wet by blood.

337
00:35:42,371 --> 00:35:43,851
What happened?

338
00:35:46,555 --> 00:35:47,965
You are wounded.

339
00:35:48,029 --> 00:35:51,013
You are wounded, Cerkutay!
We must go to the infirmary!

340
00:35:51,013 --> 00:35:53,813
Alps! Prepare the infirmary!

341
00:35:54,844 --> 00:35:56,714
It's nothing.

342
00:35:58,052 --> 00:36:00,072
The sane leaves...

343
00:36:00,890 --> 00:36:02,690
the insane stays.

344
00:36:07,136 --> 00:36:08,956
Boran.

345
00:36:11,065 --> 00:36:13,725
Boran is in the hands of
the heathens, Aygül.

346
00:36:21,645 --> 00:36:24,015
İnegöl Castle

347
00:36:26,232 --> 00:36:28,122
We'll kill you all!

348
00:36:28,163 --> 00:36:29,503
All of you!

349
00:36:35,152 --> 00:36:37,502
You gave the order, right, Rogatus?

350
00:36:39,959 --> 00:36:41,619
We will kill you too.

351
00:36:46,285 --> 00:36:47,775
Especially you!

352
00:36:48,756 --> 00:36:50,416
Demon!

353
00:36:52,206 --> 00:36:54,126
I'll have your head.

354
00:36:55,302 --> 00:36:57,602
I'll have your head!

355
00:37:00,011 --> 00:37:04,001
Even now, you are threatening
us.

356
00:37:06,132 --> 00:37:08,172
Your wife was like that too.

357
00:37:09,558 --> 00:37:12,358
She also stood tall.

358
00:37:13,862 --> 00:37:15,512
She resisted.

359
00:37:16,511 --> 00:37:18,731
But she died.

360
00:37:21,198 --> 00:37:23,268
You will share the same fate.

361
00:37:24,266 --> 00:37:27,276
Not only you, all the Turks!

362
00:37:28,018 --> 00:37:29,518
We aren't afraid of death.

363
00:37:30,518 --> 00:37:32,638
We can't drain away by dying.

364
00:37:34,124 --> 00:37:37,304
I'll be a martyr and reach to my wife.

365
00:37:39,475 --> 00:37:43,235
But I won't go anywhere
before killing you.

366
00:37:46,449 --> 00:37:48,259
He will kill us.

367
00:37:49,932 --> 00:37:51,612
Wait.

368
00:37:51,766 --> 00:37:53,326
Take a breath.

369
00:37:58,416 --> 00:37:59,906
Take a breath.

370
00:38:04,798 --> 00:38:06,408
Take a breath.

371
00:38:06,928 --> 00:38:09,028
No. No.

372
00:38:09,864 --> 00:38:12,214
I'll keep you for Nikola.

373
00:38:14,523 --> 00:38:17,393
He'll take his anger out on you.

374
00:38:19,592 --> 00:38:21,722
Until then, enjoy being here.

375
00:38:38,395 --> 00:38:40,355
Keep your eyes on him.

376
00:38:47,408 --> 00:38:49,808
Do you know how your wife died?

377
00:38:51,337 --> 00:38:52,907
Do you want me to tell you?

378
00:38:53,335 --> 00:38:54,455
Demon!

379
00:38:58,149 --> 00:39:02,149
The poison took her breath first.

380
00:39:02,369 --> 00:39:04,139
-Silence!
-Then...

381
00:39:04,638 --> 00:39:07,426
her veins exploded.

382
00:39:07,426 --> 00:39:09,046
Shut up!

383
00:39:10,057 --> 00:39:12,697
Do you know that pain?

384
00:39:14,328 --> 00:39:16,928
It's more painful than...

385
00:39:17,678 --> 00:39:19,746
you can ever imagine.

386
00:39:19,746 --> 00:39:21,106
Silence!

387
00:39:21,192 --> 00:39:22,612
She crawled...

388
00:39:24,012 --> 00:39:26,222
while agonizing.

389
00:39:26,859 --> 00:39:28,909
Shut your mouth up!

390
00:39:29,058 --> 00:39:31,188
But she was tough.

391
00:39:32,846 --> 00:39:34,856
At that condition...

392
00:39:35,095 --> 00:39:37,295
she tried to be the hero.

393
00:39:39,100 --> 00:39:41,500
And with a slice of a sword...

394
00:39:50,068 --> 00:39:51,568
she died.

395
00:39:58,498 --> 00:40:00,118
I swear that...

396
00:40:01,534 --> 00:40:06,104
I won't die before making you feel
the pain you inflicted on Gonca.

397
00:40:07,556 --> 00:40:10,596
Before taking your head off...

398
00:40:10,971 --> 00:40:13,141
the ground is haram for me.

399
00:40:13,452 --> 00:40:14,782
Haram!

400
00:40:25,617 --> 00:40:27,027
Like it wasn't enough...

401
00:40:27,689 --> 00:40:29,779
now we have his wife!

402
00:40:30,121 --> 00:40:31,401
Damn it!

403
00:40:31,573 --> 00:40:33,253
Where did they come from?

404
00:40:33,376 --> 00:40:35,106
Damn them all!

405
00:40:35,245 --> 00:40:36,765
All of them!

406
00:40:37,366 --> 00:40:39,436
Damn them!

407
00:40:39,941 --> 00:40:41,711
Where did they come from?

408
00:40:41,888 --> 00:40:43,228
Where?

409
00:40:43,381 --> 00:40:45,251
Damn them!

410
00:40:45,334 --> 00:40:48,974
Lord Kosses' dear sister Mari.

411
00:40:50,630 --> 00:40:53,910
How could you do this to me?
I'll lose my mind, Nikola!

412
00:40:54,440 --> 00:40:56,910
We'll gather our armies at once!

413
00:40:56,921 --> 00:40:59,600
Look, if it's Osman's wife who
took Mari...

414
00:40:59,600 --> 00:41:01,780
only place they'll go is Kayı Tribe.

415
00:41:02,930 --> 00:41:05,880
I'll destroy them.
All of them.

416
00:41:05,880 --> 00:41:07,560
We'll burn it.

417
00:41:07,898 --> 00:41:10,404
No one will survive. Not even
the buildings.

418
00:41:10,404 --> 00:41:13,031
I'll burn Kayı Tribe, Kosses!
I will burn it!

419
00:41:13,041 --> 00:41:16,481
Are you mad, Nikola? Will you burn
it when Mari is inside?

420
00:41:16,671 --> 00:41:18,518
I'll never allow this!

421
00:41:18,518 --> 00:41:20,047
I'll go alone to take Mari.

422
00:41:20,047 --> 00:41:22,691
What do you mean alone?
What am I?

423
00:41:22,691 --> 00:41:26,411
-She was going to be my wife!
-She will be, Nikola!

424
00:41:26,569 --> 00:41:29,899
If you attack the tribe with your army,
it will be a mess.

425
00:41:29,950 --> 00:41:32,648
It's best for you to return to
the castle and stay calm.

426
00:41:32,648 --> 00:41:35,441
What are you saying, Kosses?
They'll teach what's mine...

427
00:41:35,441 --> 00:41:37,371
and I'll stay at my castle?

428
00:41:37,435 --> 00:41:42,025
You don't understand, Nikola. If you
attack, you'll lose Mari forever!

429
00:41:44,342 --> 00:41:46,282
I'll bring you Mari.

430
00:41:46,841 --> 00:41:48,431
I promise you.

431
00:41:49,335 --> 00:41:50,885
Trust me.

432
00:41:55,146 --> 00:41:56,366
Alright.

433
00:41:57,844 --> 00:41:59,414
Go, Kosses.

434
00:41:59,646 --> 00:42:01,326
Go and take Mari.

435
00:42:02,407 --> 00:42:03,907
I'm going.

436
00:42:16,837 --> 00:42:19,337
I hope you are right.

437
00:42:30,005 --> 00:42:33,045
I hope you are right, Kosses.

438
00:42:34,207 --> 00:42:35,717
I hope so.

439
00:42:37,185 --> 00:42:38,845
Mari...

440
00:42:41,945 --> 00:42:43,625
I'm not your wife!

441
00:42:43,985 --> 00:42:45,771
I hate you!

442
00:42:45,771 --> 00:42:47,861
I hate you!
I hate you!

443
00:42:50,613 --> 00:42:52,473
Mari...

444
00:42:53,177 --> 00:42:55,477
Bring me Mari.

445
00:42:56,102 --> 00:42:57,892
Bring her...

446
00:42:58,053 --> 00:43:01,273
so that I can choke her with
my own hands.

447
00:43:02,577 --> 00:43:04,317
With my own hands.

448
00:43:10,174 --> 00:43:12,174
My condolences, Osman Bey.

449
00:43:16,434 --> 00:43:18,074
Thank you.

450
00:43:22,170 --> 00:43:24,450
The iron in those mines...

451
00:43:25,480 --> 00:43:27,970
it's wet with my martyrs' blood.

452
00:43:29,529 --> 00:43:32,829
What shield can block the attacks...

453
00:43:32,978 --> 00:43:35,148
of the swords made by that iron?

454
00:43:35,738 --> 00:43:40,258
What wall can stand against the balls
made with those iron?

455
00:43:40,446 --> 00:43:42,286
No wall, Kumral Abdal.

456
00:43:42,924 --> 00:43:44,434
No wall.

457
00:43:47,230 --> 00:43:49,540
I won't leave Boran to the heathens.

458
00:43:51,209 --> 00:43:54,829
Then, it'll be time to attack
the walls.

459
00:43:55,926 --> 00:43:59,096
Osman Bey, as long as...

460
00:43:59,877 --> 00:44:01,987
these hands have power
to hold a sword...

461
00:44:03,327 --> 00:44:05,157
I'll be with you.

462
00:44:07,983 --> 00:44:11,963
Don't worry. We won't leave
Boran to the heathens.

463
00:44:15,166 --> 00:44:16,916
May I enter, my bey?

464
00:44:17,072 --> 00:44:18,452
Come.

465
00:44:21,862 --> 00:44:24,372
My bey, Lord Kosses is here.

466
00:44:24,851 --> 00:44:26,431
He wants audience.

467
00:44:30,581 --> 00:44:32,261
Let him wait.

468
00:44:33,162 --> 00:44:34,652
As you order, my bey.

469
00:44:38,395 --> 00:44:40,945
He must be here to see his sister.

470
00:44:42,401 --> 00:44:45,521
Are we keeping here by force that we can
give her when he asks?

471
00:44:46,788 --> 00:44:48,818
I'm coming, Osman Bey.

472
00:44:49,207 --> 00:44:51,187
I have things to say.

473
00:44:51,437 --> 00:44:54,277
Turgut Bey, wait.

474
00:44:55,299 --> 00:44:57,209
Your wounds are fresh.

475
00:44:57,215 --> 00:44:58,920
Kumral Abdal will tend them.

476
00:44:58,920 --> 00:45:00,470
Take some rest.

477
00:45:00,777 --> 00:45:03,167
Let me, Osman Bey.
Let me.

478
00:45:03,460 --> 00:45:05,310
Now, Mari is with us.

479
00:45:05,999 --> 00:45:08,049
You think about the wedding date.

480
00:45:13,879 --> 00:45:15,989
I'll convince Kosses.

481
00:45:19,704 --> 00:45:21,344
But...

482
00:45:21,862 --> 00:45:23,702
don't forget that...

483
00:45:24,126 --> 00:45:27,266
our real goal is conquest.

484
00:45:31,011 --> 00:45:32,491
Alright.

485
00:45:51,840 --> 00:45:54,580
The conquests begins in the heart.

486
00:45:55,661 --> 00:45:58,311
You conquered Mari's heart.

487
00:45:59,044 --> 00:46:01,334
You saved her from the tyrants.

488
00:46:11,720 --> 00:46:13,230
Move.

489
00:46:13,279 --> 00:46:16,369
Give me your weapon first, Lord Kosses.

490
00:46:17,252 --> 00:46:19,122
Look at me, nomad!

491
00:46:19,609 --> 00:46:22,849
No one can take my sword away
from me today! Do you get it?

492
00:46:22,929 --> 00:46:24,969
Move now!

493
00:46:26,533 --> 00:46:28,203
Alps!

494
00:46:34,421 --> 00:46:36,331
Let him come with his sword!

495
00:46:55,188 --> 00:46:57,398
You are playing with fire, Osman!

496
00:46:57,499 --> 00:47:00,509
Do you think your flames are strong
enough to burn me?

497
00:47:02,191 --> 00:47:04,651
You are joining Turgut's beadledom!

498
00:47:05,594 --> 00:47:07,456
My sister was kidnapped.

499
00:47:07,456 --> 00:47:09,516
And it's your wife who did it!

500
00:47:09,944 --> 00:47:11,714
I'm here to take her.

501
00:47:12,245 --> 00:47:13,875
You will give her.

502
00:47:15,134 --> 00:47:17,134
We didn't kidnap Mari.

503
00:47:18,434 --> 00:47:21,344
And we aren't keeping her by force.

504
00:47:24,215 --> 00:47:26,715
We saved her from tyrants.

505
00:47:29,312 --> 00:47:31,562
Tyrants?

506
00:47:33,856 --> 00:47:35,536
Osman.

507
00:47:36,286 --> 00:47:38,236
She is my sister.

508
00:47:39,433 --> 00:47:41,143
I will take her.

509
00:47:42,364 --> 00:47:45,684
I will break every hand that tries
to touch my guests.

510
00:47:48,844 --> 00:47:50,544
You can be sure of that.

511
00:47:52,054 --> 00:47:54,524
Even if it's her brother.

512
00:47:59,977 --> 00:48:02,587
My fire won't burn you.

513
00:48:03,729 --> 00:48:05,799
It will be the emperor's.

514
00:48:06,564 --> 00:48:09,094
If you don't change your decision.

515
00:48:09,450 --> 00:48:13,530
I'll go to Constantinople personally
and return with the emperor's army.

516
00:48:15,244 --> 00:48:17,014
Not only the emperor...

517
00:48:18,187 --> 00:48:20,307
even if you return with the crusaders...

518
00:48:20,723 --> 00:48:22,843
I will never give Mari to you.

519
00:48:24,192 --> 00:48:28,322
Our laws never allow us to hand over
the refugees.

520
00:48:29,109 --> 00:48:32,549
That law will be the end of you
and your tribe, Osman Bey.

521
00:48:44,332 --> 00:48:46,772
Come on now.
Come to yourself.

522
00:48:48,823 --> 00:48:51,603
What did I tell you?

523
00:48:52,657 --> 00:48:57,117
Haven't I told you to marry you
to one of us when you first came here?

524
00:49:01,441 --> 00:49:05,271
You found the bravest and strongest of
them.

525
00:49:05,660 --> 00:49:07,340
Smile now.

526
00:49:09,988 --> 00:49:11,848
I'm grateful to all of you.

527
00:49:12,628 --> 00:49:14,408
If you didn't come...

528
00:49:14,603 --> 00:49:16,243
Turgut would die.

529
00:49:17,635 --> 00:49:19,235
Because of me.

530
00:49:20,492 --> 00:49:21,912
My pretty daughter.

531
00:49:22,509 --> 00:49:25,069
The bad days are in the past now.

532
00:49:25,909 --> 00:49:29,389
Now, it's time to talk about
good things, my daughter.

533
00:49:32,582 --> 00:49:36,042
I put you and your tribe in danger
by coming here.

534
00:49:36,417 --> 00:49:37,747
Mari.

535
00:49:38,300 --> 00:49:40,270
This is Kayı Tribe.

536
00:49:40,596 --> 00:49:42,746
We never abandon those
who ask for our help.

537
00:49:43,390 --> 00:49:46,540
If they come,
they will find.

538
00:49:47,529 --> 00:49:49,809
They'll want to hurt you.

539
00:49:50,369 --> 00:49:52,939
Both my brother and Nikola
won't let this slip.

540
00:49:53,365 --> 00:49:56,575
Bala is right. We are comrades
in arms now.

541
00:49:57,066 --> 00:49:58,976
Let them come.

542
00:49:59,996 --> 00:50:02,766
Take rest now.
Don't think about this.

543
00:50:03,531 --> 00:50:05,151
What if something happens to you?

544
00:50:11,151 --> 00:50:13,181
May I enter, Malhun Hatun?

545
00:50:13,543 --> 00:50:15,493
Come, Alaca.

546
00:50:20,562 --> 00:50:23,232
Malhun Hatun, Lord Kosses is here.

547
00:50:25,446 --> 00:50:27,596
He wants to see Mari.

548
00:50:30,354 --> 00:50:33,844
Shh, my girl. Be at ease.

549
00:50:34,743 --> 00:50:37,013
This is Kayı Tribe.

550
00:50:37,708 --> 00:50:41,758
As long as you don't want it, Osman Bey
won't let anyone...

551
00:50:41,758 --> 00:50:44,008
take you.

552
00:50:46,777 --> 00:50:50,017
I just lost my warriors.

553
00:50:50,837 --> 00:50:53,807
I didn't even bury them yet.

554
00:50:55,516 --> 00:50:58,376
Your dear friend Rogatus...

555
00:50:58,652 --> 00:51:00,902
is keeping one of my alps
as a hostage.

556
00:51:01,649 --> 00:51:04,129
My wrath is like great mountains!

557
00:51:06,255 --> 00:51:08,095
Now, tell me!

558
00:51:08,905 --> 00:51:14,285
Which one is scarier, the fire of
the cross or my fury?

559
00:51:16,837 --> 00:51:20,547
Turgut went beyond his limit
for the second time.

560
00:51:20,894 --> 00:51:22,724
You know it too!

561
00:51:23,782 --> 00:51:25,702
He deceived Mari!

562
00:51:26,036 --> 00:51:27,886
You can't keep her here by force!

563
00:51:27,886 --> 00:51:31,236
No one is keeping me here
by force! I stay with my free will.

564
00:51:33,463 --> 00:51:35,353
I won't return, brother.

565
00:51:39,812 --> 00:51:41,302
Mari.

566
00:51:41,596 --> 00:51:43,846
Please, don't force me.

567
00:51:45,934 --> 00:51:48,244
Let's leave here nicely.

568
00:51:48,485 --> 00:51:49,745
Never.

569
00:51:49,890 --> 00:51:51,840
I'll never come with you.

570
00:51:51,923 --> 00:51:54,723
You should've known that I wouldn't
stay where I'm ignored.

571
00:51:54,817 --> 00:51:59,317
If you don't come with me now,
I'll return with a great army.

572
00:52:01,028 --> 00:52:03,888
You will return with an army
to get your sister's corpse?

573
00:52:06,709 --> 00:52:10,419
Don't hold back. If you want
me to kill myself...

574
00:52:11,069 --> 00:52:12,499
do it.

575
00:52:13,143 --> 00:52:15,453
When you don't find what you want...

576
00:52:16,843 --> 00:52:18,963
you show your teeth.

577
00:52:20,397 --> 00:52:24,337
You come to my tribe and threaten
me with an army!

578
00:52:27,361 --> 00:52:29,151
If you have the courage...

579
00:52:29,351 --> 00:52:30,841
do it.

580
00:52:32,380 --> 00:52:35,040
Do it and see what happens!

581
00:52:36,434 --> 00:52:39,064
But I'll never give you Mari.

582
00:52:42,435 --> 00:52:45,255
-Osman...
-If you have nothing to say...

583
00:52:46,595 --> 00:52:48,245
leave now.

584
00:52:56,178 --> 00:52:59,058
As you wish, Mari.

585
00:52:59,973 --> 00:53:01,643
As you wish.

586
00:53:26,329 --> 00:53:29,499
Osman took the mine, Nikola.

587
00:53:32,994 --> 00:53:35,734
How did they get out of that
mine alive?

588
00:53:39,588 --> 00:53:42,658
Won't anything go in order today?

589
00:53:44,054 --> 00:53:45,954
How did it happen, Rogatus?

590
00:53:46,484 --> 00:53:49,204
Why does it matter?
He took it.

591
00:53:49,537 --> 00:53:54,347
But we took something he
values dearly.

592
00:53:54,777 --> 00:53:55,843
What?

593
00:53:55,843 --> 00:53:58,965
In return of the mine,
we took his most loyal alp.

594
00:53:58,965 --> 00:54:00,065
Boran.

595
00:54:00,065 --> 00:54:03,325
Finally. Finally!
Finally, good news!

596
00:54:03,590 --> 00:54:06,128
Osman loves his alps so much!

597
00:54:06,128 --> 00:54:08,278
What about Kosses?
Where is he?

598
00:54:10,961 --> 00:54:13,421
He went to take Mari.

599
00:54:24,431 --> 00:54:25,651
From Osman.

600
00:54:40,416 --> 00:54:42,526
-May I enter.
-Come.

601
00:54:54,056 --> 00:54:56,356
You shouldn't be on your feet.

602
00:54:57,602 --> 00:54:59,162
May I?

603
00:55:12,117 --> 00:55:14,047
It was a tough day for you too.

604
00:55:16,847 --> 00:55:18,577
I wanted to know if you
are alright.

605
00:55:32,024 --> 00:55:34,364
They hurt you because of me.

606
00:55:43,426 --> 00:55:46,086
I was so afraid that something
would happen to you.

607
00:55:49,015 --> 00:55:51,125
If something had happened to you...

608
00:55:51,198 --> 00:55:53,348
I would never forgive myself.

609
00:55:53,887 --> 00:55:55,447
Don't cry.

610
00:55:57,420 --> 00:56:00,590
Your pretty eyes shouldn't
be wet.

611
00:56:02,862 --> 00:56:07,322
Your tears hurt me much
more than...

612
00:56:07,589 --> 00:56:09,309
what they've done.

613
00:56:10,207 --> 00:56:11,587
Don't cry.

614
00:56:15,855 --> 00:56:17,385
Now.

615
00:56:20,018 --> 00:56:21,948
When I saw this at the market...

616
00:56:22,158 --> 00:56:23,714
it reminded me of you.

617
00:56:23,714 --> 00:56:24,854
I thought...

618
00:56:26,712 --> 00:56:28,512
I thought I could buy it
for you.

619
00:56:34,485 --> 00:56:36,255
Today is the day, it seems.

620
00:56:57,654 --> 00:56:59,254
It's so beautiful.

621
00:57:02,558 --> 00:57:04,258
And so are you.

622
00:57:10,568 --> 00:57:12,108
I'm grateful.

623
00:57:36,225 --> 00:57:37,505
Mari.

624
00:57:40,187 --> 00:57:42,157
I don't know what to say.

625
00:57:44,382 --> 00:57:45,452
You...

626
00:57:47,032 --> 00:57:48,602
did you ever think about it?

627
00:57:51,245 --> 00:57:52,805
Being...

628
00:57:59,425 --> 00:58:00,945
-May I enter?
-Come.

629
00:58:03,473 --> 00:58:06,163
Osman Bey awaits you at his tent.

630
00:58:21,415 --> 00:58:23,045
Let's go then.

631
00:58:27,807 --> 00:58:29,837
You were saying something.

632
00:58:39,382 --> 00:58:40,652
Let's go.

633
00:58:51,269 --> 00:58:54,419
İnegöl Castle

634
00:58:55,374 --> 00:58:57,494
You couldn't get Mari.

635
00:58:57,856 --> 00:58:59,246
Is that so?

636
00:59:00,343 --> 00:59:02,393
You are making no sense, Nikola.

637
00:59:04,792 --> 00:59:06,322
What are you doing?

638
00:59:06,920 --> 00:59:09,340
You ruined my reputation!

639
00:59:09,359 --> 00:59:11,229
Mari was kidnapped because
of you!

640
00:59:11,249 --> 00:59:12,997
You couldn't control a woman!

641
00:59:12,997 --> 00:59:15,838
The one you call a woman
is my sister, Nikola!

642
00:59:15,838 --> 00:59:17,913
So, stop aiming at me
with your anger!

643
00:59:17,913 --> 00:59:19,473
I won'T!

644
00:59:19,473 --> 00:59:20,503
Enough!

645
00:59:23,415 --> 00:59:24,955
We took an oath!

646
00:59:25,189 --> 00:59:28,229
We'll stay united!
We won't go after each other!

647
00:59:28,397 --> 00:59:29,897
Have you forgotten about it?

648
00:59:34,135 --> 00:59:35,785
We were going to grow together!

649
00:59:35,817 --> 00:59:37,657
We will!

650
00:59:37,768 --> 00:59:40,388
If you manage to stay calm!

651
00:59:41,013 --> 00:59:42,733
Isn't that so, Rogatus?

652
00:59:44,462 --> 00:59:48,982
We need to sit as gentlemen and
talk about how we'll take Mari back.

653
00:59:49,783 --> 00:59:51,683
You put us into this situation!

654
00:59:51,779 --> 00:59:54,229
-Is that so?
-I'll take us out!

655
00:59:54,337 --> 00:59:55,247
How?

656
00:59:55,382 --> 00:59:58,412
Father, son, the holy spirit.

657
00:59:59,977 --> 01:00:02,627
Christ will show us the way.

658
01:00:08,026 --> 01:00:10,256
Holy God!

659
01:00:10,402 --> 01:00:14,052
Did Rogatus turn you religious, Nikola?

660
01:00:14,125 --> 01:00:16,395
No! No!
It's what I've experienced.

661
01:00:18,568 --> 01:00:20,288
Someone is coming...

662
01:00:21,384 --> 01:00:23,404
to help us.

663
01:00:24,551 --> 01:00:25,981
Who?

664
01:01:01,993 --> 01:01:04,493
The Vizier of the Seljuks...

665
01:01:04,650 --> 01:01:06,450
Vizier Alemşah!

666
01:01:17,853 --> 01:01:19,523
Vizier Alemşah.

667
01:01:19,525 --> 01:01:21,045
Welcome.

668
01:01:29,530 --> 01:01:33,490
I greet the strong lords of these lands.

669
01:01:36,549 --> 01:01:41,039
But I see that you don't rule according
to your power.

670
01:01:44,666 --> 01:01:48,246
There is still chaos in your lands.

671
01:01:51,313 --> 01:01:54,843
Stability requires order.

672
01:01:56,049 --> 01:01:58,559
This order is lost, Nikola.

673
01:01:59,422 --> 01:02:04,142
You know who broke it better
than us, Vizier Alemşah.

674
01:02:10,822 --> 01:02:13,282
How will we take Boran, Osman Bey?

675
01:02:14,704 --> 01:02:18,154
In the tyrant's hands,
in a dungeon...

676
01:02:20,299 --> 01:02:23,529
I know what they are doing
to him now.

677
01:02:26,026 --> 01:02:28,276
How will we save Boran?

678
01:02:29,529 --> 01:02:31,999
What happens if he is in a dungeon?

679
01:02:34,299 --> 01:02:37,199
We'll be face to face with our Allah.

680
01:02:39,158 --> 01:02:41,348
A dungeon is seclusion for us.

681
01:02:42,853 --> 01:02:45,453
Let's say they banish us
to heathen lands...

682
01:02:46,930 --> 01:02:49,180
banish is hejira for us!

683
01:02:53,357 --> 01:02:55,347
Let's say they killed Boran...

684
01:02:56,987 --> 01:02:59,427
death is shada for us!

685
01:03:00,395 --> 01:03:02,205
It's martyrdom!

686
01:03:08,121 --> 01:03:09,751
But...

687
01:03:12,540 --> 01:03:14,970
we won't leave anyone behind.

688
01:03:16,513 --> 01:03:20,743
We'll take my brother Boran
from them.

689
01:03:22,180 --> 01:03:24,240
And we'll look forward.

690
01:03:30,270 --> 01:03:32,650
With the name of Allah.

691
01:03:34,316 --> 01:03:35,806
Go on.

692
01:03:36,318 --> 01:03:38,558
With the name of Allah.

693
01:03:40,188 --> 01:03:42,098
Enjoy it.

694
01:03:56,716 --> 01:03:59,786
My daughter, why aren't
you eating?

695
01:04:01,791 --> 01:04:03,731
My brother's threats.

696
01:04:04,028 --> 01:04:06,558
I'm afraid that he'll do something,
Selcan Hatun.

697
01:04:09,740 --> 01:04:12,730
You don't seem affected.

698
01:04:14,564 --> 01:04:16,674
We took these lands with
our blood...

699
01:04:18,428 --> 01:04:21,608
with our weapons.

700
01:04:24,500 --> 01:04:28,700
We wanted justice to reign
in our lands.

701
01:04:29,384 --> 01:04:31,254
Mercy to reign on our lands.

702
01:04:35,629 --> 01:04:39,699
If we were to give you because
of the emperor...

703
01:04:40,692 --> 01:04:42,922
as our ancestors say...

704
01:04:43,575 --> 01:04:45,835
If cruelty enters from a window...

705
01:04:46,765 --> 01:04:48,575
laws leave from the door.

706
01:04:49,182 --> 01:04:52,092
We are talking about the emperor's
army, Osman Bey.

707
01:04:52,757 --> 01:04:56,297
I know your tribe, Turgut Bey's
tribe.

708
01:04:58,441 --> 01:05:00,681
How can you stand?

709
01:05:03,925 --> 01:05:09,105
Even if your brother marches on us
with a great army, as he said...

710
01:05:10,231 --> 01:05:12,191
he can't establish superiority
against us.

711
01:05:15,918 --> 01:05:17,938
Do you think this is all of us?

712
01:05:23,989 --> 01:05:27,829
Dodurga, Yazır, Eymür, Salur...

713
01:05:28,294 --> 01:05:30,154
Bayat and Avşar.

714
01:05:30,498 --> 01:05:34,188
From Kastamonu to Dengizli,
all tribes...

715
01:05:35,734 --> 01:05:39,184
if an army had marched against us,
we'd turn into one strong fist.

716
01:05:40,197 --> 01:05:44,017
Do you know what a river is, my girl?

717
01:05:44,548 --> 01:05:46,118
Have you ever seen one?

718
01:05:47,801 --> 01:05:50,411
Do you know what a sea is?

719
01:05:51,409 --> 01:05:52,979
I do.

720
01:05:53,575 --> 01:05:57,516
When I was in Constantinople,
I would go the shore...

721
01:05:57,516 --> 01:05:59,586
and watch the sea for hours.

722
01:06:03,714 --> 01:06:04,934
Here.

723
01:06:05,795 --> 01:06:09,135
As all those rivers have one
source...

724
01:06:09,705 --> 01:06:11,475
so do we.

725
01:06:13,240 --> 01:06:17,290
As those rivers unite
in the sea...

726
01:06:17,967 --> 01:06:21,547
we unite under the
flag of Islam.

727
01:06:21,959 --> 01:06:23,869
Just like that.

728
01:06:26,786 --> 01:06:31,156
We have friendly hearts
from all cities...

729
01:06:31,472 --> 01:06:35,722
that we love,
and that love us.

730
01:06:39,481 --> 01:06:43,391
For those friendly hearts,
many battles can be fought.

731
01:06:43,714 --> 01:06:45,654
Many suffering can be endured.

732
01:06:45,816 --> 01:06:47,666
Many roads can be traveled.

733
01:06:49,444 --> 01:06:51,014
If Allah destines it...

734
01:06:52,805 --> 01:06:56,155
soon we'll go to Konya...

735
01:06:56,374 --> 01:06:58,374
for a friend of us.

736
01:06:59,687 --> 01:07:01,607
When we reach Konya...

737
01:07:01,798 --> 01:07:04,088
I'll visit Sultan Mesut too.

738
01:07:05,081 --> 01:07:06,991
As you wish, my sheik.

739
01:07:07,525 --> 01:07:10,725
Send my regard to the friends and
to Sultan Mesut.

740
01:07:11,208 --> 01:07:12,818
Alright.

741
01:07:12,978 --> 01:07:14,568
But...

742
01:07:16,649 --> 01:07:18,509
you should be at ease.

743
01:07:20,283 --> 01:07:24,243
As long as you don't want it,
no one can take you from here.

744
01:07:27,963 --> 01:07:33,023
Your courage, determination;
it's truly impressive.

745
01:07:35,915 --> 01:07:38,705
Now, Seljuks are here, lords.

746
01:07:43,963 --> 01:07:45,483
Now, tell me.

747
01:07:47,815 --> 01:07:50,515
For what do you need
my help?

748
01:07:55,410 --> 01:07:56,990
My sister.

749
01:07:57,623 --> 01:07:59,373
Vizier Alemşah.

750
01:08:00,123 --> 01:08:01,143
And...

751
01:08:03,562 --> 01:08:05,362
my future wife.

752
01:08:07,425 --> 01:08:10,675
True. She is in Osman's
tribe.

753
01:08:10,714 --> 01:08:12,964
They are keeping her there
by force.

754
01:08:13,122 --> 01:08:15,722
And if I can't take her nicely...

755
01:08:16,316 --> 01:08:19,116
I'll personally go to Constantinople...

756
01:08:19,470 --> 01:08:21,912
and ask for an army
from the emperor.

757
01:08:22,027 --> 01:08:24,006
That's not needed, Kosses.

758
01:08:27,247 --> 01:08:30,138
I'm telling you that I'll
form order here.

759
01:08:30,167 --> 01:08:33,389
There is no need to disturb
Emperor Andronikus...

760
01:08:33,389 --> 01:08:35,799
for such a small problem.

761
01:08:39,254 --> 01:08:41,084
I'll take care of it.

762
01:08:47,667 --> 01:08:49,807
Osman's alp, Boran.

763
01:08:49,966 --> 01:08:52,407
I heard that you keep him, Nikola.

764
01:08:53,934 --> 01:08:55,874
Vizier Alemşah.

765
01:08:56,063 --> 01:08:58,023
Where did you hear this from?

766
01:08:58,533 --> 01:09:00,212
Nikola.

767
01:09:00,265 --> 01:09:04,246
I know the tree that drops leaves
early...

768
01:09:04,281 --> 01:09:06,600
the river that floods late...

769
01:09:06,817 --> 01:09:09,386
and everything that's
happening in these lands.

770
01:09:16,854 --> 01:09:18,220
Boran.

771
01:09:18,220 --> 01:09:20,831
What do you plan to do with him?

772
01:10:37,810 --> 01:10:39,361
Gonca?

773
01:10:39,361 --> 01:10:40,811
Boran.

774
01:10:42,208 --> 01:10:44,588
Lay, Boran.
Lay down.

775
01:10:45,965 --> 01:10:47,635
Rest.

776
01:10:50,691 --> 01:10:52,561
You are here, huh?

777
01:10:53,829 --> 01:10:55,419
You are next to me?

778
01:10:55,584 --> 01:10:57,134
I am.

779
01:10:59,060 --> 01:11:00,910
It's too cold, Gonca.

780
01:11:02,186 --> 01:11:03,496
Too cold.

781
01:11:03,496 --> 01:11:05,556
Look at this alp of Kayı!

782
01:11:06,111 --> 01:11:08,101
What can cold do to my valiant?

783
01:11:09,528 --> 01:11:11,158
I missed you so much.

784
01:11:14,750 --> 01:11:16,710
It pains my heart.

785
01:11:19,631 --> 01:11:21,651
Please, speak a little more.

786
01:11:23,528 --> 01:11:25,108
A little more.

787
01:11:27,346 --> 01:11:29,606
I'm always cold in your absence.

788
01:11:30,834 --> 01:11:32,894
Your longing is too hard.

789
01:11:37,641 --> 01:11:39,681
It's not like any other pain.

790
01:11:40,825 --> 01:11:42,255
It doesn't go.

791
01:11:42,568 --> 01:11:44,658
Don't grow the longing...

792
01:11:45,255 --> 01:11:47,025
but the reunion, my valiant.

793
01:11:48,055 --> 01:11:49,805
Grow the reunion.

794
01:11:51,403 --> 01:11:52,953
Gonca.

795
01:11:53,672 --> 01:11:55,952
Don't leave me.

796
01:11:56,092 --> 01:11:57,992
When the time comes...

797
01:11:58,063 --> 01:11:59,823
I will leave too.

798
01:12:01,106 --> 01:12:03,206
May that time never come, Gonca.

799
01:12:06,011 --> 01:12:07,841
Don't go, Gonca.

800
01:12:09,077 --> 01:12:10,647
I beg you, don't.

801
01:12:23,940 --> 01:12:25,540
Don't leave, Gonca.

802
01:12:26,586 --> 01:12:27,806
Don't.

803
01:12:28,009 --> 01:12:29,859
I told you, Boran.

804
01:12:30,853 --> 01:12:32,673
This isn't the end.

805
01:12:33,996 --> 01:12:35,636
In the afterlife...

806
01:12:36,676 --> 01:12:38,926
we'll meet for sure.

807
01:12:44,564 --> 01:12:46,234
Don't go, Gonca!

808
01:12:51,506 --> 01:12:54,006
I beg you, don't leave.

809
01:12:59,988 --> 01:13:01,748
Gonca, stay.

810
01:13:10,433 --> 01:13:12,053
Don't go, Gonca.

811
01:13:56,809 --> 01:13:59,049
You took my sun away.

812
01:14:01,989 --> 01:14:04,599
I won't die before taking your head.

813
01:14:06,340 --> 01:14:08,170
I won't die.

814
01:14:19,520 --> 01:14:20,900
Laugh.

815
01:14:23,855 --> 01:14:26,460
I'll tie him at the square of İnegöl.

816
01:14:26,460 --> 01:14:28,022
He'll starve.

817
01:14:28,022 --> 01:14:29,412
He'll be thirsty.

818
01:14:29,422 --> 01:14:32,802
And the people will lose their
sleeps for a while, because...

819
01:14:33,146 --> 01:14:37,206
they'll listen to him agonizing.

820
01:14:40,499 --> 01:14:42,899
I'll make him an example.

821
01:14:44,173 --> 01:14:47,603
I've had the drums played all day.

822
01:14:49,608 --> 01:14:54,648
All the people will witness the death
of Osman's most loyal man.

823
01:14:58,632 --> 01:14:59,942
Good.

824
01:15:01,632 --> 01:15:04,272
But I have a better plan.

825
01:15:34,382 --> 01:15:35,722
Hera?

826
01:15:45,095 --> 01:15:46,625
What are you doing here?

827
01:15:46,960 --> 01:15:48,770
We heard it.

828
01:15:49,093 --> 01:15:50,763
Your soldiers were killed.

829
01:15:53,385 --> 01:15:55,425
I thought something happened to you.

830
01:15:57,169 --> 01:15:59,139
Thank God you are alright.

831
01:16:17,735 --> 01:16:18,865
My father.

832
01:16:19,338 --> 01:16:22,728
My father wanted me to convey an
important information to Osman Bey.

833
01:16:23,803 --> 01:16:25,373
Alright.

834
01:16:27,470 --> 01:16:29,000
Then go...

835
01:16:29,017 --> 01:16:30,437
and tell my bey.

836
01:16:31,754 --> 01:16:33,094
Alright.

837
01:16:46,339 --> 01:16:48,129
May I enter, my bey.

838
01:16:48,644 --> 01:16:50,054
Come in.

839
01:16:58,522 --> 01:17:01,472
My bey, I went after Rogatus
by your order.

840
01:17:01,833 --> 01:17:04,383
He went to İnegöl,
not to his castle.

841
01:17:08,534 --> 01:17:10,764
He is after some other treachery.

842
01:17:13,196 --> 01:17:14,456
What else?

843
01:17:16,907 --> 01:17:20,917
My bey, criers were wandering
on the square of İnegöl.

844
01:17:24,455 --> 01:17:25,995
Tell me.

845
01:17:26,307 --> 01:17:27,807
Boran Alp...

846
01:17:28,514 --> 01:17:32,404
will be killed at the square
tomorrow.

847
01:17:37,113 --> 01:17:38,843
What are you saying?

848
01:17:48,464 --> 01:17:50,244
A Turkish soldier...

849
01:17:50,576 --> 01:17:52,876
falls on the battlefield.

850
01:17:53,469 --> 01:17:55,659
Not on a city square!

851
01:17:57,642 --> 01:17:59,392
Tell all the alps!

852
01:17:59,887 --> 01:18:01,807
It's Osman Bey's order!

853
01:18:02,713 --> 01:18:04,483
We are going to İnegöl!

854
01:18:05,403 --> 01:18:06,743
As you order, my bey.

855
01:18:13,246 --> 01:18:14,976
May I enter, my bey.

856
01:18:14,997 --> 01:18:16,347
Come.

857
01:18:26,367 --> 01:18:28,037
Welcome, Hera.

858
01:18:28,909 --> 01:18:30,579
Thank you, Osman Bey.

859
01:18:31,862 --> 01:18:34,632
Are you only here to convey
your father's words?

860
01:18:37,974 --> 01:18:40,494
Aren't you sad about the passing
of my soldiers?

861
01:18:41,271 --> 01:18:43,151
Of course, Osman Bey.

862
01:18:46,060 --> 01:18:47,550
Alright, then.

863
01:18:50,883 --> 01:18:53,213
Don't be sad any longer.

864
01:18:55,337 --> 01:18:57,517
We need your help.

865
01:18:59,937 --> 01:19:01,177
Of course.

866
01:19:01,805 --> 01:19:03,855
Of course, whatever you need.

867
01:19:13,056 --> 01:19:15,336
It's good that you are here.

868
01:19:18,121 --> 01:19:20,281
We'll save Boran thanks to you.

869
01:20:06,494 --> 01:20:08,144
Saltuk said it.

870
01:20:08,200 --> 01:20:10,720
You didn't eat anything.

871
01:20:12,114 --> 01:20:14,094
Come on, Cerkutay. Eat.

872
01:20:15,786 --> 01:20:17,796
I don't want it, Aygül Hatun.

873
01:20:21,237 --> 01:20:22,687
Thank you.

874
01:20:25,044 --> 01:20:27,744
When does Cerkutay ever not
want food?

875
01:20:28,295 --> 01:20:30,615
Come on. Eat a little.

876
01:20:35,262 --> 01:20:37,602
My brother is captured
by the heathens.

877
01:20:38,312 --> 01:20:40,242
How can Cerkutay eat?

878
01:20:42,904 --> 01:20:45,034
Who knows what they are doing
to my brother.

879
01:20:45,942 --> 01:20:47,772
They are torturing Boran.

880
01:20:49,751 --> 01:20:51,321
Cerkutay.

881
01:20:51,391 --> 01:20:52,901
Don't do this.

882
01:20:53,950 --> 01:20:57,240
You said that Cerkutay is a mountain...

883
01:20:57,240 --> 01:20:59,640
no tornado can break it down.

884
01:21:00,002 --> 01:21:02,632
Now, you should stand like a mountain.

885
01:21:04,853 --> 01:21:06,403
I believe in you.

886
01:21:08,842 --> 01:21:11,682
You will get your revenge.

887
01:21:12,341 --> 01:21:14,981
And you'll bring our brother
Boran safe and sound.

888
01:21:19,188 --> 01:21:21,048
I will, huh?

889
01:21:21,956 --> 01:21:23,476
Yes, you will.

890
01:21:30,335 --> 01:21:32,155
Come on.
Come on.

891
01:21:32,204 --> 01:21:33,604
Don't let it get cold.

892
01:21:50,447 --> 01:21:52,057
Cerkutay.

893
01:21:55,237 --> 01:21:57,797
Boran is in the hands of the heathens.

894
01:22:00,037 --> 01:22:01,497
It's not the time but...

895
01:22:11,292 --> 01:22:13,682
I thought a lot, Cerkutay.

896
01:22:16,906 --> 01:22:21,536
Ever since Gonca left us, I've
been thinking.

897
01:22:23,726 --> 01:22:25,636
And the things that happened
today.

898
01:22:28,569 --> 01:22:31,269
You might not have survived
that mine.

899
01:22:33,648 --> 01:22:35,998
When I saw the martyrs
entering the tribe...

900
01:22:41,605 --> 01:22:43,275
I was so afraid.

901
01:22:47,125 --> 01:22:48,635
Death...

902
01:22:49,398 --> 01:22:51,058
is so close.

903
01:22:53,095 --> 01:22:54,915
Maybe...

904
01:22:56,461 --> 01:22:58,761
maybe it's as far away.

905
01:23:01,499 --> 01:23:03,059
What are you saying, mad girl?

906
01:23:08,679 --> 01:23:09,969
The world...

907
01:23:12,101 --> 01:23:14,111
the world doesn't last long.

908
01:23:19,561 --> 01:23:21,651
You asked me a question.

909
01:23:22,372 --> 01:23:24,052
What question--

910
01:23:31,409 --> 01:23:33,229
When did I ask it?

911
01:23:35,179 --> 01:23:37,029
Let's not wait.

912
01:23:37,229 --> 01:23:38,649
What?

913
01:23:39,530 --> 01:23:41,310
Let's marry, Cerkutay!

914
01:23:52,199 --> 01:23:54,189
Are you serious, mad girl?

915
01:23:54,890 --> 01:23:56,530
I am serious...

916
01:23:56,838 --> 01:23:58,378
mad boy.

917
01:24:29,500 --> 01:24:31,110
The secret is revealed.

918
01:24:33,512 --> 01:24:35,922
The lovers are united.

919
01:24:42,414 --> 01:24:44,464
The secret of love is patience.

920
01:24:48,814 --> 01:24:51,014
You revealed the truth, my valiant.

921
01:24:58,475 --> 01:25:01,575
May the peace, mercy, and blessings
of Allah be with you.

922
01:25:01,987 --> 01:25:04,777
May the peace, mercy, and blessings
of Allah be with you

923
01:25:19,541 --> 01:25:21,561
O' my Allah!

924
01:25:25,348 --> 01:25:27,508
You are the judge!

925
01:25:29,218 --> 01:25:33,208
Your wisdom is over anything.

926
01:25:34,744 --> 01:25:37,184
You are the owner!

927
01:25:37,839 --> 01:25:40,879
You own all there is!

928
01:25:43,842 --> 01:25:45,172
When...

929
01:25:46,519 --> 01:25:48,629
we shoot an arrow...

930
01:25:49,561 --> 01:25:53,321
we know that it's not us who
shoots it.

931
01:25:55,963 --> 01:25:58,213
It's your blessing.

932
01:26:00,125 --> 01:26:01,935
We know that...

933
01:26:02,291 --> 01:26:06,671
you broke the plans of those
who deny you.

934
01:26:07,685 --> 01:26:11,825
Destine us to be grateful
for that, my Allah.

935
01:26:14,352 --> 01:26:15,872
My Allah...

936
01:26:16,523 --> 01:26:19,163
give us strenght to...

937
01:26:19,515 --> 01:26:24,455
spread your names to all
over the earth.

938
01:26:26,145 --> 01:26:28,055
Destine us to avenge...

939
01:26:28,924 --> 01:26:31,714
our brother who fell martyrs...

940
01:26:32,588 --> 01:26:35,093
our alps who fell martyrs...

941
01:26:35,093 --> 01:26:37,793
on this holy goal.

942
01:26:39,644 --> 01:26:41,194
My Allah...

943
01:26:44,340 --> 01:26:45,940
destine us to...

944
01:26:47,709 --> 01:26:49,719
save my brother Boran...

945
01:26:51,338 --> 01:26:53,648
from the hands of the heathens.

946
01:26:58,227 --> 01:26:59,627
Amin, my Allah.

947
01:27:03,797 --> 01:27:05,567
Amin.

948
01:27:16,003 --> 01:27:17,493
Alps!

949
01:27:19,477 --> 01:27:21,427
We are going to save our brother.

950
01:27:46,738 --> 01:27:49,578
My bey, Seljuk Vizier Alemşah is coming.

951
01:28:03,790 --> 01:28:05,920
Welcome! Welcome!

952
01:28:06,898 --> 01:28:09,608
Welcome, my vizier!

953
01:30:05,215 --> 01:30:08,495
Welcome to the Kayı lands,
Vizier Alemşah.

954
01:31:19,085 --> 01:31:22,035
His eyes look evil.

955
01:31:24,338 --> 01:31:26,548
Kayı is the tree that bears
fruits...

956
01:31:26,828 --> 01:31:29,218
and he is here to stone it.

957
01:31:29,387 --> 01:31:32,757
Mother, he just arrived.
Why are you saying that?

958
01:31:33,384 --> 01:31:37,084
His gaze reminded me of Sadettin Köpek.

959
01:31:39,501 --> 01:31:42,371
He has the same treachery.

960
01:31:43,938 --> 01:31:46,180
I'm a judge of character, my girl.

961
01:31:46,180 --> 01:31:49,250
I can tell who is a warrior and
who is a traitor.

962
01:32:22,452 --> 01:32:26,462
Osman Bey, I'm here to close another era.

963
01:32:27,295 --> 01:32:30,835
It's end of the era that you acted
as you wanted.

964
01:32:31,805 --> 01:32:34,415
Complete your sentence, vizier.

965
01:32:37,163 --> 01:32:41,463
You forbid Turkmen tribes to trade
with the lords.

966
01:32:41,691 --> 01:32:45,851
And then you made a deal
with the İznik's governor.

967
01:32:47,034 --> 01:32:48,814
Whose permission did you get?

968
01:32:50,871 --> 01:32:53,961
Whose permission is needed
for doing best for the Turkmens?

969
01:32:56,580 --> 01:32:58,920
Of Konya, Osman Bey.

970
01:32:59,307 --> 01:33:00,727
Of Konya.

971
01:33:01,545 --> 01:33:05,365
Is there a free state in Konya
that I can take permission.

972
01:33:06,341 --> 01:33:08,071
Know your place!

973
01:33:12,266 --> 01:33:16,276
Taking mines, raiding places
as you want!

974
01:33:16,855 --> 01:33:19,345
What's your goal, Osman Bey?

975
01:33:20,660 --> 01:33:24,120
And you are questioning the
sovereinity of the state!

976
01:33:29,066 --> 01:33:32,176
The weapons that you will make...

977
01:33:32,191 --> 01:33:35,081
how do we know that they won't
be pointed at the Seljuks?

978
01:33:38,479 --> 01:33:40,639
Know your words!

979
01:33:48,164 --> 01:33:49,994
I respect your position!

980
01:33:51,906 --> 01:33:53,906
But know your place.

981
01:33:58,641 --> 01:34:00,511
What you talk about is treason.

982
01:34:01,179 --> 01:34:03,709
I never betray!

983
01:34:21,838 --> 01:34:24,378
It's the order of Sultan Mesud.

984
01:34:27,163 --> 01:34:30,143
For the trade and
actions you took on your own...

985
01:34:30,543 --> 01:34:33,253
without a permission...

986
01:34:33,756 --> 01:34:36,796
the taxation of the Kayı Tribe
is doubled.

987
01:35:19,724 --> 01:35:21,654
The state is here now.

988
01:35:22,794 --> 01:35:25,524
Give me a room in Söğüt.

989
01:35:26,582 --> 01:35:29,262
From now, I'll be stationed here.

990
01:35:44,042 --> 01:35:45,662
It'll be as you say.

991
01:35:48,466 --> 01:35:52,436
Onur, I want the Turkmen beys
at the inn.

992
01:35:52,555 --> 01:35:54,595
I'll talk to them.

993
01:36:00,583 --> 01:36:04,593
I want you and Turgut Bey there,
and ready.

994
01:36:07,696 --> 01:36:09,326
We'll come.

995
01:36:13,636 --> 01:36:15,806
If you don't have anything else to say.

996
01:36:17,349 --> 01:36:18,729
If you allow me...

997
01:36:19,728 --> 01:36:21,978
I have important things to do.

998
01:36:22,659 --> 01:36:25,229
Take care of your last jobs, Osman Bey.

999
01:36:25,645 --> 01:36:29,775
From now, I'll determine
what's important for you.

1000
01:37:17,777 --> 01:37:21,747
When the people is mourning for
the martyrs, he doubled the taxes.

1001
01:37:23,650 --> 01:37:25,690
We'll find a way, brother.

1002
01:37:28,058 --> 01:37:29,618
But...

1003
01:37:30,347 --> 01:37:32,647
we'll save Boran first.

1004
01:37:54,707 --> 01:37:56,467
The door.

1005
01:38:19,413 --> 01:38:22,403
These wounds are scabbed.

1006
01:38:28,467 --> 01:38:30,022
No.

1007
01:38:30,022 --> 01:38:32,002
Do you know what I'll do to you?

1008
01:38:32,206 --> 01:38:35,166
I'll tear you into pieces.
And send your pieces...

1009
01:38:35,166 --> 01:38:37,246
to your beloved Osman!

1010
01:38:37,844 --> 01:38:39,324
Craven dog!

1011
01:38:40,624 --> 01:38:42,904
Craven dog!

1012
01:38:42,904 --> 01:38:45,287
Don't worry. I won't do it right away.

1013
01:38:45,287 --> 01:38:47,650
I'll corner Osman first.

1014
01:38:47,650 --> 01:38:52,540
Having an alp like you imprisoned by
me must've driven him crazy!

1015
01:38:52,803 --> 01:38:54,203
Yes.

1016
01:38:54,341 --> 01:38:57,361
Now, he is ready to do anything.
Anything!

1017
01:38:57,552 --> 01:38:59,722
Just what I want!

1018
01:39:30,256 --> 01:39:32,106
Allahu Akbar!

1019
01:39:55,596 --> 01:39:57,666
Heathen!

1020
01:39:59,078 --> 01:40:02,598
Kill me now when you
have the chance.

1021
01:40:04,169 --> 01:40:08,309
Otherwise, sooner or later...

1022
01:40:08,782 --> 01:40:11,252
I'll take your life.

1023
01:40:12,995 --> 01:40:14,596
Turks!

1024
01:40:14,596 --> 01:40:19,076
And your empty courage!
Empty!

1025
01:40:19,582 --> 01:40:21,152
Empty!

1026
01:40:26,124 --> 01:40:27,744
Come!

1027
01:40:28,746 --> 01:40:33,296
Let's see if you'll keep your
courage when you are crucified.

1028
01:41:13,698 --> 01:41:15,138
Alps!

1029
01:41:15,677 --> 01:41:19,697
As we talked, our warriors entered
İnegöl earlier.

1030
01:41:20,214 --> 01:41:23,394
They'll gather information there.

1031
01:41:26,075 --> 01:41:27,405
But...

1032
01:41:27,541 --> 01:41:29,981
they don't even have weapons.

1033
01:41:30,929 --> 01:41:35,499
For this reason, we'll enter from
the front gates on Hera Hatun's cart.

1034
01:41:37,679 --> 01:41:39,289
The weapons will be on the cart.

1035
01:41:40,115 --> 01:41:44,295
After we enter the city,
you'll give the alps their weapons.

1036
01:41:47,497 --> 01:41:52,007
The rest depends on our
efforts.

1037
01:41:53,726 --> 01:41:56,226
We'll save our brother Boran.

1038
01:41:57,638 --> 01:41:59,358
May Allah bless our efforts.

1039
01:42:00,178 --> 01:42:02,008
As you order, my bey.

1040
01:42:12,303 --> 01:42:13,363
Come on.

1041
01:42:22,987 --> 01:42:25,247
İnegöl Castle

1042
01:43:30,208 --> 01:43:32,388
Sacred children of Byzantium!

1043
01:43:32,639 --> 01:43:34,876
The Turk you see here...

1044
01:43:35,166 --> 01:43:38,956
is the most loyal alp of Osman,
Boran Alp!

1045
01:43:44,217 --> 01:43:47,457
What did our archenemy Osman
do to us?

1046
01:43:49,218 --> 01:43:51,058
He took our village!

1047
01:43:51,719 --> 01:43:53,239
He took our mine!

1048
01:43:55,918 --> 01:43:58,932
He killed our people!
He killed you!

1049
01:43:58,932 --> 01:44:01,102
And he'll continue to do so!

1050
01:44:04,047 --> 01:44:05,287
So...

1051
01:44:08,704 --> 01:44:10,754
when Osman took our village...

1052
01:44:11,234 --> 01:44:12,554
took our mines...

1053
01:44:13,701 --> 01:44:15,261
killed you...

1054
01:44:17,565 --> 01:44:19,045
where was Boran Alp?

1055
01:44:21,892 --> 01:44:24,022
He was with Osman!

1056
01:44:24,777 --> 01:44:26,637
I will kill you.

1057
01:44:27,040 --> 01:44:28,310
What will happen now?

1058
01:44:29,155 --> 01:44:31,495
To make an example...

1059
01:44:31,602 --> 01:44:34,652
he'll be bait for birds and
animals!

1060
01:44:34,677 --> 01:44:36,827
Yes, he should be!

1061
01:44:36,827 --> 01:44:39,837
Then, it will be Osman's turn!

1062
01:44:39,837 --> 01:44:43,797
Yes, Lord Nikola!

1063
01:44:44,905 --> 01:44:48,435
He is here now.
We will do...

1064
01:44:49,681 --> 01:44:51,421
whatever you want!

1065
01:44:51,684 --> 01:44:53,054
He is yours.

1066
01:45:09,074 --> 01:45:10,804
My Allah!

1067
01:45:11,174 --> 01:45:12,414
My Allah!

1068
01:45:19,762 --> 01:45:21,742
My powerful Allah!

1069
01:45:22,029 --> 01:45:24,699
I am not going to bow down...

1070
01:45:25,180 --> 01:45:27,260
...even if they murder me right now.

1071
01:45:30,036 --> 01:45:32,946
Our prophet didn't bow down
to any difficulty.

1072
01:45:34,204 --> 01:45:35,814
I won't too!

1073
01:45:44,222 --> 01:45:45,662
I won't too!

1074
01:45:47,776 --> 01:45:50,276
If I become a martyr here...

1075
01:45:52,362 --> 01:45:53,952
I am going to witness...

1076
01:45:55,043 --> 01:45:57,623
...the vastidity of....

1077
01:45:58,240 --> 01:46:00,850
...our prophet, Allah's blessings
and peace be with him.

1078
01:46:03,475 --> 01:46:05,395
Allahu Akbar
(Allah is the greatest!)

1079
01:46:10,665 --> 01:46:12,625
Allahu Akbar
(Allah is the greatest!)

1080
01:46:36,546 --> 01:46:39,406
Where do the martyrs go?

1081
01:46:40,071 --> 01:46:41,721
To heaven.

1082
01:46:42,105 --> 01:46:47,115
Gonca Hatun, Alps, all of them
are in heaven.

1083
01:47:09,464 --> 01:47:11,154
Kayı's valiant alps!

1084
01:47:11,668 --> 01:47:13,258
What are you doing?

1085
01:47:13,382 --> 01:47:15,752
We are thinking of our martyrs,
Kumral Abdal.

1086
01:47:18,052 --> 01:47:19,672
You can answer us.

1087
01:47:20,555 --> 01:47:22,965
Do all the martyrs go the same place?

1088
01:47:33,514 --> 01:47:35,704
In Quran, it is said that...

1089
01:47:36,637 --> 01:47:40,767
"Never say that those martyred
in the cause of Allah are dead—

1090
01:47:40,767 --> 01:47:42,899
in fact, they are alive!

1091
01:47:43,448 --> 01:47:46,738
...But you do not perceive it."

1092
01:47:48,343 --> 01:47:50,313
Martyrs don't die.

1093
01:47:55,464 --> 01:47:58,074
We are going to Bedr, sons!

1094
01:48:04,906 --> 01:48:06,406
Here he is!

1095
01:48:08,138 --> 01:48:11,268
Coming as he does!

1096
01:48:12,903 --> 01:48:14,803
He is fearless!

1097
01:48:15,132 --> 01:48:18,462
Every step of him fears the enemy!

1098
01:48:19,156 --> 01:48:20,626
Look at him!

1099
01:48:21,150 --> 01:48:23,930
He beats whoever crosses his way!

1100
01:48:24,365 --> 01:48:26,215
Allah Allah!

1101
01:48:26,656 --> 01:48:31,846
Every sword wound that the lying infidels
have is made by him!

1102
01:48:36,444 --> 01:48:38,134
Who is that?

1103
01:48:38,490 --> 01:48:39,900
Do you know?

1104
01:48:40,644 --> 01:48:42,494
The master of martyrs!

1105
01:48:43,006 --> 01:48:45,496
Allah's lion Hamza!

1106
01:48:53,785 --> 01:48:57,535
Mushriks wants to take revenge.

1107
01:49:00,562 --> 01:49:03,083
Utbe's daughter Hint...

1108
01:49:03,083 --> 01:49:06,783
...assigns her slave Zenci to...

1109
01:49:07,504 --> 01:49:11,324
... take revenge for
her uncle and father.

1110
01:49:13,533 --> 01:49:17,253
She assigns her slave Wahshi...

1111
01:49:19,047 --> 01:49:21,577
...to take revenge for her uncle and father.

1112
01:49:37,816 --> 01:49:39,606
It's dusty everywhere!

1113
01:49:41,413 --> 01:49:43,153
Where is here?

1114
01:49:45,922 --> 01:49:47,552
This is Uhud.

1115
01:49:51,196 --> 01:49:52,686
My heart burns!

1116
01:49:54,856 --> 01:49:57,366
Uhud means tear!

1117
01:49:59,761 --> 01:50:01,601
The war started.

1118
01:50:04,027 --> 01:50:08,392
The Holy knows it all!
He had a dream of this!

1119
01:50:15,612 --> 01:50:17,032
Look!

1120
01:50:17,646 --> 01:50:19,036
There he is!

1121
01:50:21,173 --> 01:50:22,763
He has no shield!

1122
01:50:26,041 --> 01:50:29,401
He beats everyone in front of him
with his double sword!

1123
01:50:31,346 --> 01:50:35,136
The master of martyrs fights!

1124
01:50:35,957 --> 01:50:38,899
Mushriks are afraid of him!

1125
01:50:38,899 --> 01:50:41,939
Allah Allah!

1126
01:50:43,061 --> 01:50:45,261
Allah Allah!

1127
01:50:50,962 --> 01:50:52,452
Oh my...

1128
01:50:53,389 --> 01:50:54,749
Oh my...

1129
01:50:57,007 --> 01:50:58,707
There is someone.

1130
01:50:59,410 --> 01:51:01,060
There is someone.

1131
01:51:01,884 --> 01:51:03,634
He has a spear.

1132
01:51:03,851 --> 01:51:05,021
Wahshi

1133
01:51:06,520 --> 01:51:08,474
Don't do it, Wahshi.

1134
01:51:08,474 --> 01:51:10,654
Don't, don't!

1135
01:51:10,753 --> 01:51:14,228
Don't do it!
You'll regret!

1136
01:51:14,228 --> 01:51:16,198
Don't do it Wahshi!

1137
01:51:16,302 --> 01:51:19,172
He hid behind a rock,
watching for an oppotunity.

1138
01:51:20,426 --> 01:51:22,793
He rises his spear...

1139
01:51:22,793 --> 01:51:24,923
...throws it...

1140
01:51:25,779 --> 01:51:27,017
He shot!

1141
01:51:27,877 --> 01:51:29,687
He threw the spear!

1142
01:51:30,398 --> 01:51:31,828
He did it!

1143
01:51:33,926 --> 01:51:35,426
My Hamza is down.

1144
01:51:37,310 --> 01:51:39,020
Uhud bleeds.

1145
01:51:42,449 --> 01:51:44,989
Hadrat Hamza is down.

1146
01:51:45,112 --> 01:51:46,942
Hint stands over his head.

1147
01:51:47,210 --> 01:51:48,570
Don't!

1148
01:51:49,234 --> 01:51:52,824
My Hamza is gone!
He is gone!

1149
01:51:53,850 --> 01:51:55,940
The secret is revealed!

1150
01:51:56,767 --> 01:52:00,137
The secret is revealed!
My Hamza became a martyr.

1151
01:52:01,781 --> 01:52:03,911
How could they do this?

1152
01:52:05,085 --> 01:52:09,495
Greatly named like himself,
Mohammed is crying.

1153
01:52:11,535 --> 01:52:13,885
The secret is revealed, valiants!

1154
01:52:15,151 --> 01:52:17,331
My Hamza became a martyr.

1155
01:52:19,347 --> 01:52:21,567
My Hamza became a martyr.

1156
01:52:34,167 --> 01:52:35,787
They are not dead.

1157
01:52:36,942 --> 01:52:39,332
Don't call them dead.

1158
01:52:39,717 --> 01:52:41,367
Martyrs don't die.

1159
01:52:42,908 --> 01:52:47,098
You cannot call the martyrs dead.

1160
01:52:48,074 --> 01:52:50,674
- Martyrs don't die!
- Martyrs don't die!

1161
01:52:50,986 --> 01:52:54,196
- Martyrs don't die!
- Martyrs don't die!

1162
01:52:56,478 --> 01:52:59,968
Gonca Hatun and alps became martyr but...

1163
01:53:00,149 --> 01:53:01,809
We are still here!

1164
01:53:02,942 --> 01:53:05,882
We'll carry the banner of Kayi!

1165
01:53:06,371 --> 01:53:08,421
We will!

1166
01:53:08,803 --> 01:53:11,843
Praise be to our Allah, valiants!

1167
01:53:12,168 --> 01:53:14,098
Praise be to our Allah!

1168
01:53:42,216 --> 01:53:43,666
Stop!

1169
01:54:01,605 --> 01:54:03,065
What did you come for?

1170
01:54:10,249 --> 01:54:12,749
I am asking you, dumb!

1171
01:54:14,433 --> 01:54:17,093
We are coming from Nikea to shop
with my wife.

1172
01:54:22,860 --> 01:54:25,234
Where you are coming from doesn't matter.
Get off.

1173
01:54:25,234 --> 01:54:26,424
We'll search.

1174
01:54:27,509 --> 01:54:29,289
Search the carriage!

1175
01:54:55,587 --> 01:54:57,647
How dare you!

1176
01:55:06,857 --> 01:55:10,687
Searching the carriage of
Lord Saguros' daughter?

1177
01:55:10,977 --> 01:55:12,271
How dare you?

1178
01:55:12,271 --> 01:55:14,861
Sorry.
We misbehaved.

1179
01:55:16,789 --> 01:55:18,201
Open the way.

1180
01:55:18,201 --> 01:55:20,461
Or you'll pay dearly.

1181
01:55:22,399 --> 01:55:24,819
Soldiers!
Open the gates!

1182
01:55:53,673 --> 01:55:55,063
Let's go.

1183
01:57:13,056 --> 01:57:15,606
Gence Bey, get Alps ready.

1184
01:57:17,646 --> 01:57:19,006
Let's go.

1185
01:58:16,801 --> 01:58:19,081
I had a good Sogut tour.

1186
01:58:19,454 --> 01:58:21,454
The town planning impressed me.

1187
01:58:21,639 --> 01:58:26,269
Osman Bey is the hope for this land.

1188
01:58:26,959 --> 01:58:29,969
You are the light of Oghuz.

1189
01:58:31,296 --> 01:58:35,136
I expected a more thriving scene here.

1190
01:58:40,231 --> 01:58:42,131
I am sorry to say that...

1191
01:58:42,415 --> 01:58:45,145
...I couldn't find what
I imagined in Sogut.

1192
01:58:45,695 --> 01:58:47,385
It has many missings.

1193
01:58:48,078 --> 01:58:52,548
There is always
missings where human live.

1194
01:58:52,964 --> 01:58:54,524
But...

1195
01:58:55,259 --> 01:58:58,729
...the perfect ones see the whole.

1196
01:59:00,939 --> 01:59:05,156
The unperfect sees only the missings...

1197
01:59:05,156 --> 01:59:06,936
...in world.

1198
01:59:09,107 --> 01:59:13,477
You are absolutely right about
what you say, sheik Edebali.

1199
01:59:15,806 --> 01:59:17,986
However, seeing is not enough.

1200
01:59:19,728 --> 01:59:23,928
Our state wants Sogut to
have everything...

1201
01:59:24,537 --> 01:59:26,897
...that our state is short of.

1202
01:59:29,499 --> 01:59:33,729
Your breath shall enlight our way.

1203
01:59:35,025 --> 01:59:37,165
We want to walk together.

1204
01:59:41,365 --> 01:59:44,285
As long as our Allah lets us live...

1205
01:59:44,546 --> 01:59:46,836
...we walk in his way.

1206
01:59:49,414 --> 01:59:51,924
We like what He likes.

1207
01:59:52,388 --> 01:59:55,588
We stay away from what He dislikes.

1208
02:00:01,773 --> 02:00:03,913
We shall leave now.

1209
02:00:03,979 --> 02:00:06,103
We are going to see each other again.

1210
02:00:06,103 --> 02:00:08,333
If Allah permits...

1211
02:00:08,812 --> 02:00:10,452
...of course we will.

1212
02:00:13,866 --> 02:00:15,466
With that said...

1213
02:00:16,190 --> 02:00:20,180
We were about to leave as well.

1214
02:00:23,875 --> 02:00:26,835
We'll mention your arrival in Konya.

1215
02:00:26,961 --> 02:00:28,651
Vizier Alam Shah.

1216
02:00:31,184 --> 02:00:33,654
I would appreciate it.

1217
02:00:36,321 --> 02:00:41,551
Why are you going to Konya?

1218
02:00:43,902 --> 02:00:46,402
We are going to see a friend's face.

1219
02:00:59,713 --> 02:01:03,573
I am going to stay here.
We'll see each other when you return.

1220
02:01:08,245 --> 02:01:10,295
Go safely.

1221
02:01:11,418 --> 02:01:12,878
Eyvallah (Thanks).

1222
02:01:35,254 --> 02:01:36,534
My Sheik.

1223
02:01:36,930 --> 02:01:39,210
Do you have something in your mind?

1224
02:01:41,049 --> 02:01:44,429
Not particularly a friend visit but...

1225
02:01:45,265 --> 02:01:48,225
...we have to see Sultan Mesut.

1226
02:01:49,753 --> 02:01:51,493
As you command, my sheik.

1227
02:01:59,203 --> 02:02:02,033
He beat off every words of mine!

1228
02:02:02,792 --> 02:02:04,892
He chose his side a long time ago.

1229
02:02:08,115 --> 02:02:10,145
Go to Kosses.

1230
02:02:10,996 --> 02:02:13,938
Tell him to stop Edebali in Konya way.

1231
02:02:13,938 --> 02:02:16,828
Edebali shouldn't go to Konya, Konur!

1232
02:02:17,444 --> 02:02:20,134
Sultan Mesut should not know
what we are doing.

1233
02:05:38,658 --> 02:05:41,449
Brother!

1234
02:06:20,227 --> 02:06:21,797
Alps, trap!

1235
02:06:21,802 --> 02:06:23,102
Trap!

1236
02:06:39,032 --> 02:06:40,332
Osman Bey!

1237
02:06:52,683 --> 02:06:54,273
Ingoble dog!

1238
02:07:04,373 --> 02:07:06,263
Why would you kill Boran?

1239
02:07:06,293 --> 02:07:09,553
Is your aim to kill the pray...

1240
02:07:09,553 --> 02:07:12,433
...or to catch Osman who
will do everything to save him?

1241
02:07:17,331 --> 02:07:19,251
Vizier Alam Shah!

1242
02:07:21,386 --> 02:07:24,126
You want Osman dead too!

1243
02:07:24,687 --> 02:07:27,397
Turks don't run short of valiants, Nicola!

1244
02:07:28,332 --> 02:07:31,302
So we can sacrifice the rebel ones.

1245
02:07:33,010 --> 02:07:35,829
Captivate him, kill him,
whatever you want.

1246
02:07:35,829 --> 02:07:38,179
This is your decision.

1247
02:07:43,723 --> 02:07:45,663
What about Boran?

1248
02:07:46,128 --> 02:07:48,408
When Osman comes to save Boran...

1249
02:07:48,863 --> 02:07:50,823
there will be someone
else in place of him.

1250
02:07:51,833 --> 02:07:56,093
And you'll trap him with your soldiers.

1251
02:07:58,690 --> 02:08:00,750
Vizier Alam Shah.

1252
02:08:01,422 --> 02:08:05,312
I am glad to have common objectives.

1253
02:08:06,881 --> 02:08:09,191
I'll trap Osman.

1254
02:08:22,274 --> 02:08:24,014
Can I come in?

1255
02:08:24,429 --> 02:08:25,699
Come.

1256
02:08:35,558 --> 02:08:37,228
Welcome.

1257
02:08:51,634 --> 02:08:53,524
You are hurt.

1258
02:08:54,034 --> 02:08:56,354
You are lucky to have me here.

1259
02:08:57,028 --> 02:09:00,048
You are alive and in front of me
thanks to me.

1260
02:09:10,656 --> 02:09:13,936
If your fate was up to Osman Bey...

1261
02:09:14,545 --> 02:09:18,225
...we would be having your funeral now.

1262
02:09:49,801 --> 02:09:51,821
Hello, Edebali!

1263
02:09:51,821 --> 02:09:53,911
Where are you going without my permission?

1264
02:10:12,254 --> 02:10:16,734
The creator of this way and
our body is Allah.

1265
02:10:17,818 --> 02:10:22,188
If He wants us to go,
even the whole world cannot stop us.

1266
02:10:24,134 --> 02:10:26,424
If He doesn't want us to go...

1267
02:10:27,256 --> 02:10:30,826
...even all the ways are opened,
we can't arrive.

1268
02:10:32,185 --> 02:10:33,765
Is that so?

1269
02:10:34,014 --> 02:10:36,064
Let's ask Him.

1270
02:10:43,381 --> 02:10:46,721
No.
Your God doesn't want you to go today.

1271
02:10:49,200 --> 02:10:50,620
Soldier!

1272
02:10:51,000 --> 02:10:52,580
Attack!

1273
02:11:23,368 --> 02:11:24,948
My Sheik!

1274
02:11:36,157 --> 02:11:38,047
Soldier!

1275
02:12:40,532 --> 02:12:43,042
When the dog barks relying on
the number of them...

1276
02:12:43,736 --> 02:12:46,156
...the wolf choke them!

1277
02:12:49,643 --> 02:12:51,433
You outnumber us...

1278
02:12:52,379 --> 02:12:54,349
...but we are Turks!

1279
02:13:04,212 --> 02:13:15,422
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com